# Day 36 - Find Missing and Repeated Values

## Problem Statement
You are given a `0`-indexed `n × n` integer matrix `grid` containing values in the range `[1, n²]`.

Each integer appears exactly once except:
- One integer `a` appears **twice**.
- One integer `b` is **missing**.

Return a 0-indexed integer array `ans` of size `2` where:
- `ans[0]` is the repeated value `a`.
- `ans[1]` is the missing value `b`.

## Code

class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> findMissingAndRepeatedValues(vector<vector<int>>& grid) {
        unordered_set<int> s;
        vector<int> ans;

        int n = grid.size();
        int a, b;
        int actualSum = 0, expSum = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                actualSum += grid[i][j];

                if (s.find(grid[i][j]) != s.end()) {
                    a = grid[i][j];
                    ans.push_back(a);
                }
                else {
                    s.insert(grid[i][j]);
                }
            }
        }

        expSum = (n * n) * ((n * n) + 1) / 2;
        b = expSum + a - actualSum;

        ans.push_back(b);

        return ans;
    }
};

